# Images and other binary assets must never go through CRLF normalization,
# regardless of a contributor's core.autocrlf setting. Without this, a binary
# file can be silently corrupted on checkout depending on git's line-ending
# heuristics (this repo runs with core.autocrlf=true locally).
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary
*.gif binary
*.svg binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Source and config files stay LF regardless of checkout platform.
* text=auto eol=lf
